    "result_text": "There's now an \"Export people (CSV)\" button (`data-testid=\"export-people\"`) on the People section, and it downloads `people.csv`. All 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\nThe whole change is in the front end, in `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people.ts`. The browser builds the file from the values the list already shows, so it needed no server, database or audit changes. The file contains:\n\n- **Header:** `name,grade,retired-from,due-total`.\n- **Rows:** everyone in list order, including retired people even when \"Show retired\" is off.\n- **Values:** the grade in force on the sheet's today, the retired-from date or nothing, and the due-total exactly as the row shows it (`n/a` included).\n- **Quoting:** a value with a comma, a double quote or a line break is wrapped in double quotes, with any quotes inside doubled. Every line, including the last, ends with a line feed.\n\nOne consequence of building it in the browser: the file reflects what this screen has loaded. Changes another user has made since then only appear after the sheet is re-loaded, the same as the list itself.",
